# Architecture Sketch

How Drive, Claude, the API and the scheduler connect.

![Architecture diagram](architecture.svg)

## Components

| Component | Role |
|---|---|
| Trainer Central | Emails the trainer when a participant submits an assignment |
| Trainer's Google Drive folder | The trainer saves each email as a separate `.txt` file |
| Windows Task Scheduler | Starts `app.py` every 30 minutes with no manual trigger |
| `app.py` (my laptop) | Orchestrates each run |
| Claude API | Reads one email, decides if it is mine, returns JSON details |
| `state.db` (SQLite) | Remembers processed Drive file IDs so nothing is posted twice |
| Dashboard API (Render) | Receives entries via `POST /api/entries` |
| `logs/run.log` | Records files seen, files matched and API status for every run |

## Flow of one run

1. Task Scheduler starts `app.py`.
2. The app lists the `.txt` files in the Drive folder and skips file IDs already in `state.db`.
3. For each new file, the text and `prompt.txt` go to Claude, which returns JSON: `is_mine`, assignment name, submission time, status, other details.
4. If the email is not mine or the file is empty, it is recorded as processed and skipped.
5. If it is mine, the app calls `GET /health` (Render wakes slowly), checks the dashboard for the file's `[drive-file:<id>]` marker, then calls `POST /api/entries` with `sender` = my name.
6. On success the file is recorded in `state.db`. On a Claude or API failure it is left unrecorded and retried on the next run.
7. The run summary is written to `logs/run.log`.

## Text diagram

```
Trainer Central --> Drive folder (.txt) --+
                                          v
Task Scheduler (30 min) --> app.py --> Claude API (is mine? + JSON)
                              |  ^
                              |  +--- state.db (processed files)
                              v
                     Dashboard API (POST /api/entries)
                              |
                              +--- logs/run.log
```
